From 51772bed10c1a6e645eda8c8f1deac7464803838 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:05:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Multi-CPU MADT, virtio-blk driver, smp-blk self-test recipe

For Composite simple_vmm's multi-vCPU and virtio-blk support:

- vmxbooter: list as many CPUs in the MADT as the VMM reports (CPUID leaf
  0BH subleaf 1, core level), up to MAX_CPU = 16, when running under
  simple_vmm (hypervisor bit + its ACRN CPUID signature); one CPU
  anywhere else, as before. The I/O APIC entry now follows the last
  local APIC entry, and the MADT is zeroed as a whole (the memset used
  sizeof of the pointer).
- defconfig: CONFIG_BLK_DEV, CONFIG_VIRTIO_BLK and CONFIG_EXT2_FS, so
  every image can use the VMM's virtio-blk disk as /dev/vda.
- recipes/smp-blk: boots into a self-test that checks all CPUs came
  online, runs one worker per CPU, and does a raw write/read-back and an
  ext2 mkfs/mount/remount round trip on /dev/vda, printing SMPBLK
  PASS/FAIL lines, then gives a shell.

Tested under plain QEMU (TCG, -smp 2, QEMU's legacy virtio-blk-pci):
SMPBLK DONE: 0 failure(s). Not tested under simple_vmm (needs VT-x).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YA4RSTF4ZQjZipvcZwi7Rv
